<title>GERMANY: Continental's profits jump.</title>
<headline>Continental's profits jump.</headline>
<dateline>BONN, Germany</dateline>
<text>
<p>German tire-maker Continental AG said Wednesday its pre-tax profits jumped 62 percent in the first nine months of the year.</p>
<p>The company said pre-tax earnings to the end of September surged to 125 million marks ($83.26 million) from 77 million, while sales rose 2.6 percent to 7.63 billion marks ($5.1 billion).</p>
<p>Continental attributed the improvement to gains from lower-cost production achieved by moving some of its operations out of Germany and Ireland to Portugal, the Czech Republic and France.</p>
</text>
